OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Automations/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group. The repo's real,
compiled canonical page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/` — proven by every DONE
sibling page (AutomationsListPage, AutomationActivityFeedPage, ActionBuilderPage, … all under
Sources/Features/<Domain>) and by xcodegen (project.yml `- path: Sources`, shared by the iOS +
macOS app targets, ADR-002). The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Automations/**`; its XCTest ships at
`apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Automations/**`; strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the only deviation from
the literal prompt path — identical to the DONE sibling ActionBuilder's reconciliation.

REUSE / DRY (engineering principles — no duplication of the proven domain core):
The pure, Foundation-only projection layer for this surface already ships, module-public, in the
P4 feature-view (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/TriggerConfigurator.{Adapter,Catalog,Model}.swift`):
the discriminated `AutomationTrigger` union + `TriggerKind` + `createDefault`, the `SignalTrigger`/
`SignalValue`/`SimpleSchedule` shapes, `CronExpression.build`/`.parse`, `TriggerAdapter`
(`toggleDay`/`isDayActive`/`signalValue`/`displayValue`/`parseLeadingDouble`/`numberString`), the
`Geofence` wire model, the option catalogs (`VehicleEventCatalog`/`GeofenceEventCatalog`/
`SignalOperatorCatalog`/`SignalCatalog`/`TimezoneCatalog`/`WeekdayCatalog`/`TriggerTypeCatalog` +
`TriggerOption`), `TriggerConfiguratorAccessibility`, and the geofence-query projection
(`GeofenceInput`/`GeofenceResolved`/`GeofenceProjection`). This unit REUSES that core (one source of
truth, zero type collisions — new symbols are all `TriggerConfiguratorPage*`) and feeds it a
`Localizable.xcstrings` localizer, then ships a fresh page/model/views that resolve every string from
the platform catalog (the P7 string requirement). No feature-views file was edited (out of scope).

NAVIGATION (the unit is (unrouted)):
The web `TriggerConfigurator` is a controlled SECTION the `/automations` builder renders inline and
switches on `trigger.kind` — NOT a standalone route. So this unit does NOT take a top-level `AppRoute`
(that would hijack a sibling unit's route). Instead it ships a typed `NavigationDestination` seam —
`TriggerConfiguratorPageLink` + `View.triggerConfiguratorDestination()` +
`TriggerConfiguratorPageRouteRegistration.make(...)` — that any `NavigationStack` adopts to deep-link
the full-screen trigger editor. As a standalone screen it adds the trigger-TYPE selector its web
parent owns, so all four kind editors are reachable; switching seeds the web `createDefaultTrigger`.
No edits to the P4 shell (AppShell/AppRoute/TeslaSyncApp) — correct for an unrouted unit (covenant #7).

